any such element. Its J7 is a 1x03 debug UART header.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The battery terminals should only be connected through the battery holder, the protection diode path and the DC-jack switch contact. A header across BAT+ and BAT- is not part of the documented power architecture. If it is a power jumper it would be an undocumented battery short when fitted.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(comp (ref \\\"J7\\\")\\n      (value \\\"Conn_02x01\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"9\\\") (name \\\"NET0011\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\")\\n      (node (ref \\\"J7\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pinfunction \\\"Pin_1\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"J7\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pinfunction \\\"Pin_2\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"| J7 | Conn_01x03 | Debug UART header | netlist: pin1\u2192GND, pin2\u2192`UART_TX` (SKW92A pin 26), pin3\u2192`UART_RX` (SKW92A pin 25) |\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"If the jumper is fitted, the 18650 cell is shorted through a low-resistance path, which is a serious safety hazard and drains the battery. If it is unfitted, it is dead copper with no function, and the spec's J7 debug-UART identity is inconsistent with the netlist.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.4\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist contains a capacitor (C10) placed on an inductor footprint with one terminal floating, and a 2-pin header (J7) that is not in the specification and bridges the battery positive and negative terminals. Both are inconsistent with the documented design. Confidence is moderate because the J7 jumper may be an intentional, unlisted option.\"\n}",
